<LessonLayout title="Catechist's Guide &mdash; The Virtues" cic="CCC 1803-1845" scripture="">

<section class="content">

<h2>Catechist's Guide</h2>
<p class="big-question">For preparing and leading the class.</p>

<h3>Class Summary</h3>

<p><strong>Estimated time:</strong> 60 minutes</p>
<p><strong>Core topic:</strong> Virtues are habitual dispositions to do good. The cardinal virtues are acquired through practice; the theological virtues are received as gifts from God.</p>
<p><strong>Objectives:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Understand what a virtue is and how it is acquired.</li>
<li>Identify the four cardinal virtues and their importance.</li>
<li>Distinguish the theological virtues from the cardinal virtues.</li>
<li>Know the gifts and fruits of the Holy Spirit.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Key verse:</strong> &laquo;Put on compassion, kindness, humility, meekness, and patience&raquo; (Col 3:12)</p>
<p><strong>Catechism references:</strong> CCC 1803-1845</p>

</section>

